      "questionNumber": "5.4",
      "dependsOn": ["math_g12_chain_rule_001"],
      "questionText": "Find f'(x) using the chain rule.",
      "marks": 3,
      "partOfChain": true,
      "chainId": "calculus_derivatives_nov_2023_p2"
    },
    "sprintData": {
      "questionText": "Given f(x) = (3x² + 2x - 1)⁴, find f'(x) using the chain rule.",
      "providedContext": {
        "f(x)": "(3x² + 2x - 1)⁴",
        "rule": "Chain rule: d/dx[g(h(x))] = g'(h(x)) × h'(x)",
        "concept": "Composite function differentiation"
      },
      "marks": 4,
      "canRandomize": true,
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "estimatedTime": 5,
      "tags": ["calculus", "derivatives", "chain_rule"]
    },
    "correctAnswer": "f'(x) = 4(3x² + 2x - 1)³(6x + 2)",
    "answerVariations": [
      "f'(x) = 4(3x² + 2x - 1)³(6x + 2)",
      "4(3x² + 2x - 1)³(6x + 2)",
      "f'(x) = 4(6x + 2)(3x² + 2x - 1)³",
      "4(6x + 2)(3x² + 2x - 1)³",
      "f'(x) = (6x + 2) × 4(3x² + 2x - 1)³"
    ],
    "caseSensitive": false,
    "answerType": "algebraic",
    "grade": 12,
    "subject": "mathematics",
    "topic": "calculus_derivatives",
    "cognitiveLevel": "Level 3",
    "workingSteps": [
      "Given: f(x) = (3x² + 2x - 1)⁴",
      "Let u = 3x² + 2x - 1, so f(x) = u⁴",
      "Apply chain rule: f'(x) = d/dx(u⁴) × du/dx",
      "d/dx(u⁴) = 4u³",
      "du/dx = d/dx(3x² + 2x - 1) = 6x + 2",
      "Therefore: f'(x) = 4u³ × (6x + 2) = 4(3x² + 2x - 1)³(6x + 2)"
    ],
    "hints": [
      "Identify the outer and inner functions",
      "Apply the chain rule: d/dx[g(h(x))] = g'(h(x)) × h'(x)",
      "The derivative of (3x² + 2x - 1) is 6x + 2"
    ],
    "explanation": "Using the chain rule for f(x) = (3x² + 2x - 1)⁴, we get f'(x) = 4(3x² + 2x - 1)³ × (6x + 2)",
